      "body": "> > For anyone who sees this thread in the future.\n> > \n> > Using `--dnssleep 120` is the way and only way to disable doh checks.\n> > \n> > We need to know how long we have to wait before we can continue to get the cert.\n> > \n> > We have two ways: 1. we check dns records by doh checks. or 2. just use a `--dnssleep 120` time.\n> \n> You said `--dnssleep 120` is the way and **only way** to disable doh checks.But in https://github.com/acmesh-official/acme.sh/issues/2576#issuecomment-550582048 you said `--dnssleep 180`  and in https://github.com/acmesh-official/acme.sh/issues/2587#issuecomment-553922985 you also said \"Try with “`—dnssleep 300`\".What is the determined value? Do you mind elaborating why a sleep does prevent the doh call? I have read the code but still can't find the code like `300`,`180`,`120`.\n\n@awslblog the value is totally arbitrary.\nIt's just a timeout waiting for your name servers to update/sync the new txt record ",
